Howdy,

My most promising Slash'em character to date, Alec the Addled the
droven wizard, just bit it at 27th level.  I'd done significant
reading on Demogorgon, as I've never had to deal with him before, and,
for some reason, I thought I was prepared...

After finding his level (right below Juiblex', the second down from
the Valley), I made a couple mistakes.  I didn't know exactly when
he'd jump me - if he'd teleport to me as I wandered the maze, of if I
had to get into his sight line - so I wasn't sure when to fully prep,
given that there are a fair amount of other monsters on the level.  I
should've gone back up the stairs and dropped my bag of holding to
unburden myself, and I should've alt'ed to just my hands, as my
strategy was to put him to sleep and then freeze him to death.  (I
also wasn't sure if you could still pay demon lords off or not - guess
not?)

Anyway, I found a muddy area with a vrock at the entrance with a
'5' (warning) a few squares back.  I hit the vrock with my +7 Deep
Freeze and confuse monster, and it stepped away and Demogorgon
teleported in, hit me, and stung me.  OK, deep breath, we expected
this.  Heal with blessed +7 unicorn horn.  He hits me, stings me
twice, and does something else, maybe curses me?  I heal again, and
now I get a turn.  He's already hit me for half my hit points, but I'm
not panicking.  I'll just teleport over to the stairs like I'm
supposed to...  "A mysterious force prevents you from teleporting.
Demogorgon cast a spell!  A pool of water appears under your feet!
You sink like a stone!  You attempt to teleport to safety.  Your
attempt fails.  You die."  (Or words to that effect.)  WTF!

I'm playing on my iPhone, so I'm not entirely sure that's what
happened, as there's no easy way to go back and look at the messages
once you're dead.  But I'm very sure my attempt to teleport - the only
non-heal action I took - failed and I got no further actions.  I've
looked back at all the spoilers and I see no indication that
Demogorgon's level is unteleportable or undiggable.  I don't see any
power that he has that suppresses teleport.  And I don't get why he
can teleport, but apparently I couldn't?  Is there a big hole in the
spoilers?

Also, the whole pool of water thing blows!  I wasn't aware of that
spell's existence, and it seems entirely overpowered.  I had both
boots of water walking and an amulet of flying, but I was wearing
either reflection or drain resistance at that point, as I didn't
realize that spellcasters had an instakill preventable only by ability
to negotiate water!  (Though apparently you get a last ditch teleport
attempt IF YOU'RE NOT ON A $&/^ing NO TELEPORT LEVEL!)

Anyway...  Other lessons learned:

 - Vecna dies when hit with two dozen plus acid streams.
 - Artifact weapons will break just like regular ones when used to
force locks!  (My poor Magicbane!)
 - Air elementals + lava can lead to serious problems...  (My poor +5
speed boots!)
 - Flaming/freezing spheres are not a good idea around peaceful
priests...  (My poor ring of TC!)
 - Nightmare should not be attacked with magic; Elbereth and +4
bullets are the way to go.  (My poor amulet of life saving!)

(It was a triumphant Chaotic Quest and a Nightmarish Lawful Quest.)

Otherwise, I cast stone to flesh successfully exactly once - on the
statue of a previous incarnation of my character who thought it'd be a
good idea to punch a cockatrice in the face with no gloves on.  After
killing myself (the stone-to-fleshed me, that is) I got a ton of loot
of my corpse.  Given that I had, like an 86% chance of failure and not
much power it was pretty lucky that I got it on my one and only try.

Anhur kept helpfully giving me shit I did not need, including Deluder,
Deep Freeze, Stormbringer, two hellhounds, two bar-igura, and a barbed
(?) devil.  The former two pets died in the melee on the Chaotic
quest.  The two devilish ones I had at that point survived the Chaos.
One went peaceful while hanging out in the Lawful Quest area and was
later killed when I remembered why wielding Stormbringer is a dumb
idea.  The remaining two were mowed down by Disgruntled Adventurers
and/or angelic beings, both of which jumped me around the same time.

I marooned both Yeenoghu and Juiblex in the Dungeons after sacrificing
elves.

The Dark One was upset that I called him a punk - he summoned nasties
the second I entered his room this time, getting both a master mind
flayer AND an arch-lich (plus a silver dragon, a Jabberwock, and a rot
worm).  I teleported to the up stairs, he followed me, I hit him with
my hands, he went to sleep.  Just before I could finish him off, the
lich teleported in too.  I Elberethed and tried out my wand of undead
turning, which did nothing useful; he summoned nasties and got a
minotaur and some other jank.  I hit the Dark One again, killing him,
bounced around a bit to draw everyone away from the stairs, and then
teleported back to the stairs, grabbed the goods (Eye, Bell) and
escaped upstairs.  I didn't go back until I'd throne genocided master
mind flayer and blessed scroll nuked L.  Nuking from orbit is the best
and only way to deal with L, IMO.

All in all a pretty good game for starting with a droven wizard and
getting sleep and resist poison.  I usually just quit if I don't get
force bolt, but I gave it a go and it worked out OK.  The game really
didn't want me going the 'usual' route, though.  I didn't get magic
missile tech until I BOUGHT it from One-Eyed Sam!  (For 10k gold!)  I
also blew 50k gold on a magic lamp from him that failed to give me the
Wallet of Perseus, presumably due to all the artifact junk Anhur had
stuck me with.  I did shoplift Serpent's Tongue fairly early on,
though, so maybe it was just karma.

Thanks,
Alex


